WEBVTT

00:00:07.360 --> 00:00:10.990
-The city...
-Our city...

00:00:43.020 --> 00:00:46.440
Altair: A Record of Battles

00:01:57.130 --> 00:02:02.640
It seems that we played right into the Imperials' hand.

00:02:03.220 --> 00:02:05.140
The Imperial deserters

00:02:05.310 --> 00:02:07.690
and the Imperial ship that infiltrated the harbor,

00:02:07.850 --> 00:02:11.310
it was all a decoy to distract us

00:02:11.480 --> 00:02:15.320
from the land army
attacking us from the crystal cliffs.

00:02:15.490 --> 00:02:19.610
A meticulous plan backed by
a suicide squad capable of doing the impossible.

00:02:19.780 --> 00:02:23.660
We had already lost this war
from the very beginning.

00:02:26.000 --> 00:02:27.580
Will Phoinike...

00:02:28.500 --> 00:02:29.670
...fall?

00:02:30.750 --> 00:02:33.800
The Sinking City

00:02:33.960 --> 00:02:36.420
Don't be a fool, Nikephoros!

00:02:36.590 --> 00:02:41.430
Phoinike cannot fall.

00:02:41.800 --> 00:02:45.930
This kingdom has stood for 3000 years.

00:02:46.100 --> 00:02:50.440
It has been protected by the Great Wall
and the Great Lighthouse.

00:02:50.600 --> 00:02:54.650
That's right, it's not over yet.

00:02:54.860 --> 00:02:58.530
Close off the southern walls,
and gather as many soldiers as you can.

00:02:58.650 --> 00:03:01.450
We will stand and face the Imperial army here.

00:03:01.610 --> 00:03:04.410
This is not over.

00:03:04.580 --> 00:03:07.330
Do not fall for the Empire's
cowardly psychological tactics.

00:03:07.500 --> 00:03:10.750
If we make our stand here
and wait for the Venedik Armada to arrive...

00:03:12.380 --> 00:03:13.750
What is this?

00:03:14.750 --> 00:03:16.250
Magistros.

00:03:16.920 --> 00:03:19.170
I've flooded the voice pipes with water.

00:03:19.340 --> 00:03:21.260
I think this is far enough.

00:03:22.300 --> 00:03:25.640
We should raise the white flag
and surrender to the Imperial army.

00:03:25.810 --> 00:03:28.350
What have you done, Kaisaras?

00:03:28.560 --> 00:03:31.270
Do you have any idea what you've just done?!

00:03:31.480 --> 00:03:35.270
What I've done? Do you still not see
the reality we are facing here?

00:03:35.440 --> 00:03:37.570
If we choose to fight them to the bitter end,

00:03:37.730 --> 00:03:41.280
every Phoinikian in the city would be slaughtered.

00:03:41.490 --> 00:03:43.450
Even if this were a righteous cause,

00:03:43.610 --> 00:03:47.370
if it means the extinction of the Phoinike people,

00:03:47.540 --> 00:03:50.500
-then it's time we abandoned such ideals.
-Don't be ridiculous!

00:03:50.660 --> 00:03:54.380
-A nation without ideals is--
-Then you can fight this war on your own.

00:03:54.540 --> 00:03:58.880
Stop dragging Phoinike into your
own personal ideals.

00:04:01.760 --> 00:04:04.760
In honor of the Phoinikian Senate traditions of old,

00:04:04.930 --> 00:04:11.060
I call the matter of ending our war
with the Empire to a vote.

00:04:11.230 --> 00:04:17.060
All in favor of surrendering to the Empire.

00:04:24.740 --> 00:04:26.320
Then...

00:04:28.280 --> 00:04:30.540
I will take responsibility for this!

00:04:31.290 --> 00:04:34.080
Stop it. This is not your responsibility.

00:04:37.080 --> 00:04:42.090
I am Kaisaras. All responsibility falls to me.

00:04:45.800 --> 00:04:48.640
They have raised the flag of surrender.

00:04:48.810 --> 00:04:51.140
When I first heard this plan from Lord Glalat,

00:04:51.310 --> 00:04:55.310
-I had my doubts of its success.
-Indeed.

00:04:55.480 --> 00:05:00.940
Without even stepping outside his room
in Castle Michael,

00:05:01.110 --> 00:05:05.530
Minister Louis managed to topple this city,
which had been impregnable for 3000 years.

00:05:05.700 --> 00:05:08.120
It won't be long before the Centro

00:05:08.280 --> 00:05:13.000
and the whole of Rumeriana belongs
to the Balt-Rhein Empire.

00:05:13.790 --> 00:05:16.040
I am here to relay the Senate's decision!

00:05:16.210 --> 00:05:19.170
On this day, Year 3,022 of the Phoinikian calendar,

00:05:19.340 --> 00:05:21.630
Year 451 of the Imperial calendar,

00:05:21.840 --> 00:05:23.420
on the 29th day of the fifth month,

00:05:23.590 --> 00:05:27.050
Phoinike hereby submits to the Balt-Rhein Empire

00:05:27.220 --> 00:05:29.890
a formal and complete surrender.

00:05:32.850 --> 00:05:35.890
It is a wise decision.

00:05:41.610 --> 00:05:45.030
Get back to our ship.
We need to pull back to the harbor.

00:05:45.280 --> 00:05:50.700
I repeat, Phoinike submits to the Balt-Rhein Empire
a formal and complete surrender.

00:05:50.870 --> 00:05:54.370
All men, lay down your arms,
and gather to the harbor.

00:05:55.330 --> 00:05:58.830
My house is on fire. My wife and child were there...

00:05:59.000 --> 00:06:01.920
Grandma, please, don't be dead.

00:06:02.090 --> 00:06:03.130
All right, let's go.

00:06:03.340 --> 00:06:05.300
-Hurry. We need to get back.
-Hurry.

00:06:07.720 --> 00:06:09.340
Imperial deserters,

00:06:09.510 --> 00:06:13.060
there are military medic stations
located along the castle walls.

00:06:13.510 --> 00:06:15.850
Go and disguise yourselves as Phoinikian soldiers.

00:06:19.400 --> 00:06:20.650
I wish you luck.

00:06:29.450 --> 00:06:33.200
I've done what I can, but you should take him
to a doctor as soon as possible.

00:06:33.370 --> 00:06:34.910
Okay.

00:06:35.580 --> 00:06:36.700
Kiros.

00:06:36.870 --> 00:06:38.080
Right.

00:06:38.660 --> 00:06:42.540
I'll be smuggling Mahmut Bey out of the city now.

00:06:44.090 --> 00:06:47.130
Don't worry, as soon as I get him to safety,
I'll be right--

00:06:47.300 --> 00:06:48.590
Don't bother coming back.

00:06:51.220 --> 00:06:53.390
While you're out,

00:06:53.550 --> 00:06:56.310
we'll take care of the city for you.

00:06:56.470 --> 00:07:00.060
You've got something else you want to do, don't you?

00:07:00.230 --> 00:07:03.150
Kiros, you've always wanted to leave.

00:07:03.310 --> 00:07:04.860
See the outside world.

00:07:05.610 --> 00:07:07.860
Only come back

00:07:08.030 --> 00:07:10.860
when you're ready to take our country
back from the Empire.

00:07:12.870 --> 00:07:13.950
You're right.

00:07:14.660 --> 00:07:16.370
Mahmut Pasha.

00:07:16.580 --> 00:07:20.250
-Please, take care of Kiros for us.
-Bring him back in one piece.

00:07:20.370 --> 00:07:22.540
Mahmut Pasha.

00:07:45.900 --> 00:07:50.570
Am I only imagining
that flag of surrender flying behind you?

00:07:51.070 --> 00:07:53.200
I have one thing to say to you all.

00:07:53.360 --> 00:07:55.240
If you continue your ways,

00:07:55.410 --> 00:07:57.990
then your Empire will fall.

00:07:58.160 --> 00:07:59.910
You only need to look at history.

00:08:00.080 --> 00:08:05.210
-The reason Phoinike boasts 3000 years of glory is--
-Shut up already, you loser.

00:08:06.880 --> 00:08:08.420
With people and nations,

00:08:08.590 --> 00:08:12.220
the only ones with the right to prosper
are the ones with power.

00:08:12.430 --> 00:08:14.680
No matter how grand your ideals are,

00:08:14.840 --> 00:08:17.050
no matter how long your history is,

00:08:17.220 --> 00:08:21.390
they won't help you survive.

00:08:21.560 --> 00:08:24.020
The only thing that matters is power!

00:08:24.440 --> 00:08:25.440
You're wro--

00:08:31.860 --> 00:08:34.200
No, you're wrong.

00:08:34.360 --> 00:08:38.740
I will never accept Balt-Rhein.

00:08:38.910 --> 00:08:42.160
However, the reason my beloved
Phoinike is engulfed in flames

00:08:42.370 --> 00:08:44.000
is because of me.

00:08:44.170 --> 00:08:47.630
I was the one who set it ablaze.

00:08:48.880 --> 00:08:50.710
Honestly.

00:08:50.880 --> 00:08:53.220
Even when the city is burning down around you,

00:08:53.380 --> 00:08:55.970
you get to die, still drunk on your own ideals.

00:08:56.140 --> 00:08:59.180
What a lucky man.

00:09:13.110 --> 00:09:16.740
May 29th, Year 75 of the Torqye Calendar
The Phoinike War Ends

00:09:30.840 --> 00:09:34.300
It's safe now, Mahmut Bey.

00:09:51.730 --> 00:09:54.400
Just hold on a little longer, Mahmut Bey.

00:09:54.570 --> 00:09:57.860
We'll be able to reach a nearby port in three hours.

00:09:58.450 --> 00:10:00.780
We'll find a doctor as soon as we arrive.

00:10:06.580 --> 00:10:08.830
A black cross on the sails,

00:10:09.000 --> 00:10:11.130
and the flag of the black wolf.

00:10:11.290 --> 00:10:13.460
The Venedik Armada?

00:10:14.300 --> 00:10:18.220
Capitan, I believe that is the small boat
that was in the report.

00:10:19.640 --> 00:10:23.010
Once we commandeer the vessel,
turn the ship about-face.

00:10:23.890 --> 00:10:25.560
We will return to Venedik.

00:10:26.020 --> 00:10:27.520
Aye, aye.

00:10:40.660 --> 00:10:44.660
I am Capitan of the Venedik Armada, Silvestro Brega.

00:10:45.120 --> 00:10:47.830
Mahmut Bey of the Torqye Stratocracy,

00:10:48.000 --> 00:10:51.960
and Kiros Ios Apollodorus of Phoinike,

00:10:52.170 --> 00:10:55.920
in accordance to the Venedik-Phoinike alliance,

00:10:56.090 --> 00:10:58.130
I hereby offer you both asylum here

00:10:58.300 --> 00:11:00.930
on the Venedik Armada flagship, the Nero Lupo.

00:11:01.470 --> 00:11:03.930
We will show you to the sick bay right away.

00:11:06.560 --> 00:11:08.560
There is something I'd like to ask you.

00:11:08.770 --> 00:11:12.400
Why did Venedik break their oath with Phoinike?

00:11:12.560 --> 00:11:18.030
We did not break our oath. We followed our pledge,
and our assembly agreed to send reinforcements

00:11:18.190 --> 00:11:21.530
when we received the request
from Phoinike for support.

00:11:21.700 --> 00:11:24.410
After securing the provisions and personnel,

00:11:24.580 --> 00:11:28.410
we set sail for these waters
as fast as humanly possible.

00:11:28.580 --> 00:11:32.920
What good are reinforcements
if they don't join the battle?

00:11:33.080 --> 00:11:34.960
I'm sorry to interrupt,

00:11:35.130 --> 00:11:37.920
but I request that Mahmut Bey
be treated immediately.

00:11:38.590 --> 00:11:40.630
You can pick a fight with them later.

00:11:40.800 --> 00:11:42.380
You'll die at this rate.

00:11:42.890 --> 00:11:44.010
Bey.

00:11:44.680 --> 00:11:46.930
Why did you leave Phoinike to burn?

00:11:47.850 --> 00:11:49.270
Stop.

00:11:50.680 --> 00:11:53.730
Why? Why did you not...

00:11:54.440 --> 00:11:56.230
...try to save us?

00:11:59.110 --> 00:12:00.530
Bey.

00:12:00.690 --> 00:12:02.530
Hurry. Bring the stretcher here.

00:12:05.120 --> 00:12:07.160
Capitan, take him to my quarters.

00:12:07.370 --> 00:12:09.250
Where will you stay then, Abiriga?

00:12:09.950 --> 00:12:14.000
I will bunk with my men.

00:12:41.240 --> 00:12:42.950
Why does it all burn?

00:12:43.610 --> 00:12:45.110
Why does history repeat?

00:12:45.280 --> 00:12:48.450
Do my choices not matter?

00:12:48.620 --> 00:12:51.450
No, I must have made a mistake somewhere.

00:12:51.620 --> 00:12:54.290
But where? Where did I go wrong?

00:12:54.870 --> 00:12:58.130
Venedik's Doge Lucio is a personal friend of mine.

00:12:58.290 --> 00:13:02.300
He is not the kind of man who would break an oath.

00:13:02.920 --> 00:13:04.260
He trusted him.

00:13:05.130 --> 00:13:08.640
-Was he not supposed to trust him?
-But this time was merely a coincidence.

00:13:09.140 --> 00:13:14.850
It's not because your actions were correct
that everything happened to work out.

00:13:16.020 --> 00:13:17.560
That's right.

00:13:17.730 --> 00:13:19.900
Individuals and nations have different issues.

00:13:20.730 --> 00:13:22.570
Even between nations,

00:13:22.740 --> 00:13:27.870
is forging relationships on trust
not the key to diplomacy?

00:13:28.620 --> 00:13:30.990
Am I in the wrong?

00:13:31.660 --> 00:13:33.290
I don't know.

00:13:35.370 --> 00:13:36.870
I hear bells.

00:13:55.850 --> 00:13:59.100
Mahmut Bey, how do you feel?

00:14:04.400 --> 00:14:07.240
I've brought food for Iskandar.

00:14:09.530 --> 00:14:12.240
Whoa, there, I'm not an enemy here.

00:14:15.910 --> 00:14:17.540
All right, all right.

00:14:17.710 --> 00:14:19.210
I'll just set it down here.

00:14:20.710 --> 00:14:21.750
Why?

00:14:22.380 --> 00:14:27.930
How can the crew and the Capitan act so calmly?

00:14:28.090 --> 00:14:30.930
After abandoning Phoinike for ruin.

00:14:32.050 --> 00:14:33.390
Honestly...

00:14:33.560 --> 00:14:36.270
They don't seem to have any emotion at all.

00:14:36.430 --> 00:14:40.850
My guess is that most people from Venedik
are like that.

00:14:42.440 --> 00:14:43.900
Well, you'll have to excuse me.

00:14:44.110 --> 00:14:47.070
Seeing that Iskandar seems to be in a foul mood too.

00:14:47.280 --> 00:14:50.110
I'll go do my job as kulak
and see if I can rustle up anything.

00:14:56.330 --> 00:14:58.250
The queen of the Centro,

00:14:58.410 --> 00:14:59.620
the people of Venedik...

00:15:27.610 --> 00:15:30.900
The history of Venedik?

00:15:41.170 --> 00:15:43.670
Capitan, it is Abiriga.

00:15:43.830 --> 00:15:46.380
-Come in.
-Excuse me.

00:15:51.470 --> 00:15:55.890
I received word that the Phoinikian Magistros
was killed by an Imperial soldier.

00:16:05.900 --> 00:16:07.860
What's that supposed to be?

00:16:08.030 --> 00:16:10.360
What's the point of mourning them now?

00:16:10.530 --> 00:16:13.990
I merely followed the Capitan's orders.

00:16:14.200 --> 00:16:16.370
I'd ask you what you're doing here as well.

00:16:16.950 --> 00:16:18.620
You don't need to sneak around.

00:16:18.790 --> 00:16:21.330
If you want to ask a question, go ahead and ask.

00:16:29.420 --> 00:16:31.420
Magistros is dead?

00:16:33.800 --> 00:16:37.100
His blood is on Venedik's hands.

00:16:37.260 --> 00:16:40.850
The lanky one offered flowers to the sea.

00:16:41.020 --> 00:16:44.480
But he was only following orders.

00:16:44.650 --> 00:16:45.770
It was just for show.

00:16:46.860 --> 00:16:49.980
I told you, I'm not an enemy.

00:16:53.650 --> 00:16:56.950
Kiros, do you know the head of Venedik,

00:16:57.120 --> 00:16:58.950
Doge Lucio?

00:16:59.740 --> 00:17:02.200
I think I met him when I was a kid.

00:17:02.370 --> 00:17:07.960
Since they were allies, most foreign visitors that would
come to the house would be Venedik politicians.

00:17:08.130 --> 00:17:11.960
It's just my impression as a kid, but
all they seemed to talk about was business.

00:17:12.130 --> 00:17:14.300
They only cared about national interest.

00:17:14.470 --> 00:17:19.760
It's clear now that they only viewed this alliance
as nothing more than a verbal agreement.

00:17:19.930 --> 00:17:23.770
Some even call the Doge the Fox of the Centro.

00:17:33.780 --> 00:17:38.410
Venedikian glass is made from Phoinikian crystal.

00:17:39.160 --> 00:17:44.410
Venedik exports many other products
made from the crystal.

00:17:44.580 --> 00:17:47.080
The two nations have had a long history together.

00:17:47.250 --> 00:17:51.210
And 200 years ago, they formed their alliance.

00:17:51.380 --> 00:17:54.210
Phoinike supported Venedik's trade and economy,

00:17:54.380 --> 00:17:57.590
while Venedik offered military support
to Phoinike in return.

00:17:58.140 --> 00:18:00.180
That was the oath.

00:18:03.640 --> 00:18:07.560
Did the Doge have something
more important than trust to answer to?

00:18:07.730 --> 00:18:09.770
What could that be?

00:18:09.940 --> 00:18:12.980
What did the Doge choose over trust?

00:18:32.380 --> 00:18:34.630
Year 75 of the Torqye calendar.

00:18:34.800 --> 00:18:36.340
June 7th.

00:18:36.510 --> 00:18:38.760
Nine days since coming aboard the ship.

00:18:39.470 --> 00:18:42.390
We should be arriving to Venedik soon.

00:18:55.230 --> 00:18:56.740
Mahmut Bey.

00:19:11.710 --> 00:19:13.540
I am thankful to you

00:19:13.710 --> 00:19:17.260
for your warm care and hospitality
despite my insolence.

00:19:17.420 --> 00:19:21.130
-It seems you've recovered quite a bit.
-Yes.

00:19:21.300 --> 00:19:24.550
Capitan Brega, I have come to ask you a favor.

00:19:24.720 --> 00:19:26.310
When we arrive to Venedik,

00:19:26.470 --> 00:19:28.890
I would like an audience with the Doge.

00:19:29.060 --> 00:19:32.520
I am interested in meeting
and speaking with him directly.

00:19:32.690 --> 00:19:34.060
I understand.

00:19:34.230 --> 00:19:38.400
I have already sent word to the Doge
of your presence.

00:19:38.570 --> 00:19:42.280
The Doge would very much like to meet you as well.

00:19:42.820 --> 00:19:45.620
I shall take you to his official residency myself.

00:19:45.780 --> 00:19:47.830
Thank you very much.

00:19:50.120 --> 00:19:51.790
We can see it now.

00:19:54.170 --> 00:19:55.540
Mahmut Bey,

00:19:55.710 --> 00:19:58.460
I don't know what you're planning on doing,

00:19:58.630 --> 00:20:01.010
but I'll be seeing this through to the end.

00:20:01.130 --> 00:20:04.050
I'm curious to see what kind of Pasha you'll become.

00:20:04.970 --> 00:20:08.770
I've put my life in your hands, after all.

00:20:24.950 --> 00:20:27.990
Wow, this is amazing.

00:20:28.160 --> 00:20:31.040
To think that this used to be nothing.

00:20:31.160 --> 00:20:34.120
This is my first time seeing this place too.

00:20:35.290 --> 00:20:40.210
-We will head to his official residency once we dock.
-Okay.

00:20:46.340 --> 00:20:49.430
Venedik was built by immigrants.

00:20:49.640 --> 00:20:55.600
Five hundred years ago, equestrian tribes
drove our Venedikian forefathers to these lands.

00:20:55.770 --> 00:20:59.610
Ever since then, people of many creeds
displaced by civil war and oppression

00:20:59.730 --> 00:21:02.150
slowly began to gather here.

00:21:02.690 --> 00:21:05.110
They claimed this land which could only grow reeds,

00:21:05.280 --> 00:21:07.200
and carved out a city for themselves.

00:21:07.370 --> 00:21:11.410
I understand that the city has been
divided by the five elemental deities:

00:21:11.580 --> 00:21:14.120
water, fire, metal, tree, and earth.

00:21:14.290 --> 00:21:15.620
I'm impressed you knew that.

00:21:15.790 --> 00:21:20.250
Oh, no. I simply read that in a book
I found in your room.

00:21:20.420 --> 00:21:22.050
I see.

00:21:22.210 --> 00:21:25.010
I'm sure to those who had lost their homelands

00:21:25.180 --> 00:21:28.140
it was more convenient
to divide themselves by the five elements

00:21:28.300 --> 00:21:30.140
than it was to do it by race or creed.

00:21:30.680 --> 00:21:35.980
My own roots can be traced back
to the water worshipers of Tharros Kingdom,

00:21:36.100 --> 00:21:37.850
so I live in the water district.

00:21:38.610 --> 00:21:39.860
Tharros?

00:21:40.020 --> 00:21:43.030
I believe I have not introduced myself yet.

00:21:43.610 --> 00:21:45.030
I am Abiriga.

00:21:45.200 --> 00:21:48.620
I lead Brega Company's private militia.

00:22:04.920 --> 00:22:08.050
Doge, allow me to be blunt.

00:22:08.840 --> 00:22:14.770
Why did you betray the alliance
between Phoinike and Venedik?

00:23:48.740 --> 00:23:52.200
The people of Venedik are rational realists.

00:23:52.360 --> 00:23:54.280
Is that all it is?

00:23:54.450 --> 00:23:55.780
Or is it something else?

00:23:55.950 --> 00:23:58.660
Next time, "Masquerade of Sincerity."

00:23:58.830 --> 00:24:01.250
A bell rings to signal the raising of the curtains.

00:24:01.370 --> 00:24:02.540
Masquerade of Sincerity
